From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:25:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] ubox: logd: copy the log into the new buffer when it
 grows

When the log buffer grows, logd moves the destination past each copied
entry from the old entry's address, so from the second entry on it
copies into the old buffer, frees that buffer, and keeps pointing into
it.

Add a patch to ubox that moves past each copy in the new buffer. It is
meant for ubox upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/system/ubox/Makefile                  |  2 +-
 ...he-new-buffer-when-it-copies-the-log.patch | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/system/ubox/patches/101-logd-advance-in-the-new-buffer-when-it-copies-the-log.patch

diff --git a/package/system/ubox/Makefile b/package/system/ubox/Makefile
index 541b814..6b1e3f4 100644
--- a/package/system/ubox/Makefile
+++ b/package/system/ubox/Makefile
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=ubox
-PKG_RELEASE:=3
+PKG_RELEASE:=4
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=$(PROJECT_GIT)/project/ubox.git
diff --git a/package/system/ubox/patches/101-logd-advance-in-the-new-buffer-when-it-copies-the-log.patch b/package/system/ubox/patches/101-logd-advance-in-the-new-buffer-when-it-copies-the-log.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..33cfb07
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/system/ubox/patches/101-logd-advance-in-the-new-buffer-when-it-copies-the-log.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] logd: advance in the new buffer when it copies the log
+
+When the log buffer grows, log_buffer_init() copies the entries into the
+new buffer, but it moves the destination past each copy by the size of
+the old entry from the old entry's address. From the second entry on it
+therefore copies into the old buffer, which it frees afterwards, and
+leaves newest pointing into the freed buffer.
+
+Move past each copy in the new buffer.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/log/syslog.c
++++ b/log/syslog.c
+@@ -345,7 +345,7 @@
+ 		l = log_list(0, NULL);
+ 		while ((start < end) && l && l->size) {
+ 			memcpy(start, l, PAD(sizeof(struct log_head) + l->size));
+-			start = (struct log_head *) &l->data[PAD(l->size)];
++			start = (struct log_head *) &start->data[PAD(start->size)];
+ 			l = log_list(0, l);
+ 		}
+ 		free(log);
